# Drive identity is the ID, not the name

Google Drive allows many files or folders with the same name in one parent. Each is a different ID. Markdown Pro must never create a second `Markdown-pro` root, a second sibling folder, or a second `.md` file just because a name lookup was skipped.

## Rules

- Before `files.create` for a folder or markdown file, query that parent for `name + trashed = false` (and folder mime, or not-folder for files).
- If one or more hits exist, reuse the canonical ID. Update file content on that ID. Do not POST another item.
- If several hits share the same parent, merge extras into the canonical item (move folder children; for files keep one and delete the rest). Do not park extras in a `Markdown-pro 2` wrapper folder.
- Only merge duplicates that share the same parent. A nested folder that happens to be named `Markdown-pro` is not a second app root.
- `ensureRootFolder` must reconcile same-parent `Markdown-pro` folders even when localStorage already has a valid folder ID. A stored ID is a cache, not proof there is only one root.
- `createFolder` / `createFile` are get-or-create. Callers must not list-then-create as a second uniqueness path.

## Do not

- Treat `listFiles().find(name === x)` as sufficient uniqueness. That misses pagination and races. Query by name in the Drive API, then create only if zero hits, then query again.
- Short-circuit root ensure on a cached ID without a periodic same-name search.
- Suffix user-visible names (`aimonger (2)`) to dodge collisions. Absorb into the existing ID instead.
